msgid "Native SQL queries with Quarkus Data"
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr "Essa tecnologia é considerada {extension-status}."

msgid ""
"In _experimental_ mode, early feedback is requested to mature the idea.\n"
"There is no guarantee of stability nor long term presence in the platform until the solution matures.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid "For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr "Para obter uma lista completa de possíveis status, consulte nosso https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ]."

msgid ""
"Sometimes you need full control over the SQL sent to the database, or need to use database-specific SQL syntax that is not portable across databases.\n"
"This guide shows you how to write native SQL queries in Quarkus using `@NativeQuery` annotations and Java records, with compile-time generated implementations.\n"
"The examples work directly with query results and do not require entity classes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also use native SQL with mapped entities.\n"
"See the xref:quarkus-data-hibernate.adoc#repositories[Quarkus Data Hibernate reference guide] for repository queries with entities, or the xref:quarkus-data-hibernate-getting-started.adoc[Getting Started with Quarkus Data Hibernate] guide to learn about entity mapping."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "Pré-requisitos"

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr "Para concluir este guia, você precisa:"

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr "Cerca de 15 minutos"

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr "Um IDE"

msgid "JDK {jdk-version-earliest}+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr "Apache Maven {maven-version}"

msgid "A working container runtime (Docker or xref:podman.adoc[Podman])"
msgstr "Um container runtime instalado (Docker ou xref:podman.adoc[Podman])"

msgid "Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr "Opcionalmente, o xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] se você quiser usá-lo"

msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introdução"

msgid ""
"You're working on a physical bookstore website, in which you want users to be able to browse books with titles.\n"
"In this tutorial, we won't deal with the frontend and the user interface, we just want to connect to the database."
msgstr ""

msgid "We'll start this tutorial by creating a new empty Quarkus application:"
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI"
msgstr "CLI"

msgid "To create a Gradle project, add the `--gradle` or `--gradle-kotlin-dsl` option."
msgstr "Para criar um projeto Gradle, adicione a opção `--gradle` ou `--gradle-kotlin-dsl`."

msgid "For more information about how to install and use the Quarkus CLI, see the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] guide."
msgstr "Para obter mais informações sobre como instalar e usar a CLI do Quarkus, consulte o guia xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI]."

msgid "Maven"
msgstr "Maven"

msgid "To create a Gradle project, add the `-DbuildTool=gradle` or `-DbuildTool=gradle-kotlin-dsl` option."
msgstr "Para criar um projeto Gradle, adicione a opção '-DbuildTool=gradle' ou '-DbuildTool=gradle-kotlin-dsl'."

msgid "For Windows users:"
msgstr "Para usuários do Windows:"

msgid "If using cmd, (don't use backward slash `\\` and put everything on the same line)"
msgstr "Se estiver usando cmd, (não use barra invertida '\\' e coloque tudo na mesma linha)"

msgid "If using Powershell, wrap `-D` parameters in double quotes e.g. `\"-DprojectArtifactId={create-app-artifact-id}\"`"
msgstr "Se estiver usando o Powershell, envolva os parâmetros '-D' entre aspas duplas, por exemplo, '\"-DprojectArtifactId={create-app-artifact-id}\"'"

msgid "Then let's import the extensions:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first dependency, `quarkus-data-hibernate`, provides Quarkus Data Hibernate's database access APIs and integration with Quarkus.\n"
"The second dependency, `quarkus-jdbc-postgresql`, is the JDBC driver that tells Quarkus how to talk to a PostgreSQL database.\n"
"This tutorial uses blocking database access, which requires a JDBC driver.\n"
"For other databases, choose the corresponding `quarkus-jdbc-*` driver (see xref:datasource.adoc#configure-a-jdbc-datasource[Configure a JDBC datasource]) and adapt the SQL initialization script below to that database's syntax."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Configuração"

msgid ""
"Quarkus Data Hibernate uses the Quarkus Data annotation processor, which reads your repository interfaces at compile time and generates implementation classes.\n"
"These generated classes are compiled together with your code and wired up automatically by Quarkus. They are also simple to read, in case you want to understand how it works internally."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable it, add the annotation processor configuration to your build file.\n"
"For Maven, merge the configuration into the existing `maven-compiler-plugin` entry:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Now run xref:continuous-testing.adoc[Quarkus continuous testing] from the project directory in a separate tab of your terminal:"
msgstr ""

msgid "If you are not using the Quarkus CLI, run `./mvnw quarkus:test` with Maven or `./gradlew quarkusTest` with Gradle."
msgstr ""

msgid "You don't need to restart Quarkus testing, it will re-run tests continuously after every change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Database initialization"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Since we're writing raw SQL without entity mapping, we'll create the schema and sample data ourselves.\n"
"Create a `schema.sql` file in `src/main/resources/`.\n"
"Hibernate ORM automatically runs this script during schema initialization in dev and test modes."
msgstr ""

msgid "This SQL script creates sequences for ID generation and the `Publisher` and `Book` tables."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Next, create a `data.sql` file in `src/main/resources/` to load the sample data.\n"
"Hibernate ORM automatically runs this script after schema initialization in dev and test modes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This SQL script inserts sample data.\n"
"Each book is linked to a publisher.\n"
"The final statements set each sequence to the largest imported ID, so the next generated ID follows the sample data even if you add more rows to the script."
msgstr ""

msgid "See xref:hibernate-orm.adoc#sql-init-scripts[SQL init scripts] for more details about schema and data initialization."
msgstr ""

msgid "Querying data"
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a file called `Library.java` in the package `org.acme` to query books by title:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A repository interface that groups all your query methods for books. The annotation processor generates the implementation for you."
msgstr ""

msgid "A Java record that maps to the columns returned by the SQL query. The selected columns match the record components in name and type."
msgstr ""

msgid "`@NativeQuery` sends raw SQL to the database. The `:title` syntax is a named parameter, it avoids SQL injection attacks."
msgstr ""

msgid "The method signature defines the parameters."
msgstr ""

msgid "We can now create a test in `src/test/java/org/acme/LibraryTest.java` that will check everything is working correctly:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`@QuarkusTest` starts the full Quarkus application for the test, including the database and Dev Services. The data from `data.sql` is loaded automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "We inject our `Library` just like we would in application code."
msgstr ""

msgid "We query for a book we know exists in `data.sql` and verify it's returned."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you have continuous testing running in another terminal, these tests will run automatically as soon as you save the file."
msgstr ""

msgid "Updating data"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Native SQL can also modify rows without mapped entities.\n"
"Add an `updatePrice` method to `Library`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The method returns the number of updated rows.\n"
"Both arguments are bound as query parameters, just as in the title query."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Write operations require a transaction.\n"
"In application code, invoke the repository from a CDI bean method annotated with `jakarta.transaction.Transactional`; see xref:transaction.adoc[Using transactions in Quarkus]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For the test, use `@TestTransaction` to run the update and verification in a transaction that is rolled back after the test.\n"
"This keeps the sample data unchanged for other tests and subsequent continuous-testing runs.\n"
"Add this import to `LibraryTest`:"
msgstr ""

